// Module `map`: Map[K: key, V], own, insertion-ordered (SEM-5).
// Field legend and GROWTH, FREEZE, CORE: API.md, "Reading a contract"; the layout and
// the tombstone and compaction rule: API.md, "Map and Set".
//
// Representation: 24-byte header inline; one storage block of capacity x (size(K) +
// size(V) + 16), rounded up to 8 (MEM-26), charged to the limit where the map was made
// (MEM-28). The 16 bytes per entry pay for its 8-byte hash and two 4-byte index slots (the index
// has twice the entry capacity). GROWTH doubles capacity from 4 entries. Equality and hash are the key type's
// own (SEM-5, R11): two maps hash and compare keys alike exactly when their key types are
// the same type. `for (k, v) in m` binds views of each live key and value in insertion
// order (G13) and FREEZES m for the loop.

/// CORE. An empty map with no storage. Ex: `let mut m: Map[String, u64] = map.new()`
pub fn new[K: key, V]() -> Map[K, V]

/// An empty map with storage for n entries.
/// Fails: Error(c). Alloc: n x (size(K) + size(V) + 16) rounded to 8, current limit.
/// Ex: `let mut index: Map[String, u64] = map.with_capacity(64)?`
pub fn with_capacity[K: key, V](n: u64) -> Result[Map[K, V], Capacity]

/// CORE. Number of live entries. Cost: O(1). Ex: `map.len(m)`
pub fn len[K: key, V](m: Map[K, V]) -> u64

/// CORE. A view of k's value, or None. View: anchored to m; FREEZE m.
/// Cost: expected O(1); O(len) when keys collide (the hash is fixed and unseeded).
/// Ex: `match map.get(m, w) { Some(v) => v, None => 0 }`
pub fn get[K: key, V](m: Map[K, V], k: K) -> Option[View[V]] in m

/// Whether k is present. Cost: as get. Ex: `map.contains(seen, k)`
pub fn contains[K: key, V](m: Map[K, V], k: K) -> bool

/// CORE. Adds (k, v) at the end of the order; when k is present, replaces its value in
/// place, keeps the stored key and its position, cleans the old value, then drops k.
/// When the entry array is full: compacts in place if at least half its slots are
/// tombstones (no admission), else grows (GROWTH; the copy also drops tombstones).
/// Fails: Error((c, k, v)) when growth is refused; m unchanged.
/// Alloc: GROWTH only. Cost: amortised O(1); a growing or compacting call is O(capacity).
/// Ex: `map.insert(mut m, take key, take value)?`
pub fn insert[K: key, V](mut m: Map[K, V], take k: K, take v: V) -> Result[(), (Capacity, K, V)]

/// Calls f with the value of k in place and returns Some of f's result; None when k is
/// absent, without calling f. The entry-style update: no key copy, no allocation.
/// f must not reach m (it is lent for the call). A failure in f propagates; the value
/// keeps whatever f installed. Alloc: nothing. Cost: as get, plus f.
/// Ex: `if map.update(mut counts, w, fn(mut n: u64) { n += 1 }) == None { map.insert(mut counts, take string.copy(w)?, take 1)? }`
/// PROVISIONAL (F15): as list.sort; f gets the same summaries and must not wait.
pub fn update[K: key, V, R](mut m: Map[K, V], k: K, f: scoped fn(mut V) -> R) -> Option[R]

/// CORE. Removes k and returns its value; the stored key is cleaned. The entry becomes a
/// tombstone, so the remaining entries keep their order. Alloc: nothing; storage kept.
/// Cost: as get. Ex: `let old = map.remove(mut index, k)`
pub fn remove[K: key, V](mut m: Map[K, V], k: K) -> Option[V]

/// Cleans every entry in insertion order; keeps storage. Cost: O(capacity).
/// Ex: `map.clear(mut m)`
pub fn clear[K: key, V](mut m: Map[K, V])
